H2600.definition:
from H2580 (חֵן);
gratis, i.e. devoid of cost, reason or advantage
KJV: without a cause (cost, wages), causeless, to cost nothing, free(-ly), innocent, for nothing (nought, in vain.

H2601.definition:
probably by orthographical variation for H2606 (חֲנַנְאֵל);
Chanamel, an Israelite
KJV: Hanameel.

H2602.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
perhaps the aphis or plantlouse
KJV: frost.

H2603.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2583 (חָנָה));
properly, to bend or stoop in kindness to an inferior; to favor, bestow; causatively to implore (i.e. move to favor by petition)
KJV: beseech, [idiom] fair, (be, find, shew) favour(-able), be (deal, give, grant (gracious(-ly), intreat, (be) merciful, have (shew) mercy (on, upon), have pity upon, pray, make supplication, [idiom] very.

H2604.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2603 (חָנַן);
to favor or (causatively) to entreat
KJV: shew mercy, make supplication.

H2605.definition:
from H2603 (חָנַן); favor;
Chanan, the name of seven Israelites
KJV: Canan.

H2606.definition:
from H2603 (חָנַן) and H410 (אֵל); God has favored;
Chananel, probably an Israelite, from whom a tower of Jerusalem was named
KJV: Hananeel.

H2607.definition:
from H2603 (חָנַן); gracious;
Chanani, the name of six Israelites
KJV: Hanani.

H2608.definition:
or חֲנַנְיָהוּ; from H2603 (חָנַן) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has favored;
Chananjah, the name of thirteen Israelites
KJV: Hananiah.

H2609.definition:
of Egyptian derivation;
Chanes, a place in Egypt
KJV: Hanes.

H2610.definition:
a primitive root;
to soil, especially in a moral sense
KJV: corrupt, defile, [idiom] greatly, pollute, profane.

H2611.definition:
from H2610 (חָנֵף);
soiled (i.e. with sin), impious
KJV: hypocrite(-ical).

H2612.definition:
from H2610 (חָנֵף);
moral filth, i.e. wickedness
KJV: hypocrisy.

H2613.definition:
feminine from H2610 (חָנֵף);
impiety
KJV: profaneness.

H2614.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2596 (חָנַךְ));
to be narrow; by implication, to throttle, or (reflex.) to choke oneself to death (by a rope)
KJV: hang self, strangle.

H2615.definition:
probably from H2603 (חָנַן); favored;
Channathon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hannathon.

H2617.definition:
from H2616 (חָסַד);
kindness; by implication (towards God) piety; rarely (by opposition) reproof, or (subject.) beauty
KJV: favour, good deed(-liness, -ness), kindly, (loving-) kindness, merciful (kindness), mercy, pity, reproach, wicked thing.

H2618.definition:
the same as H2617 (חֵסֵד); favor;
Chesed, an Israelite
KJV: Hesed.

H2619.definition:
from H2617 (חֵסֵד) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has favored;
Chasadjah, an Israelite
KJV: Hasadiah.

H2621.definition:
from H2620 (חָסָה); hopeful;
Chosah, an Israelite; also a place in Palestine
KJV: Hosah.

H2623.definition:
from H2616 (חָסַד);
properly, kind, i.e. (religiously) pious (a saint)
KJV: godly (man), good, holy (one), merciful, saint, (un-) godly.

H2624.definition:
feminine of H2623 (חָסִיד);
the kind (maternal) bird, i.e. a stork
KJV: [idiom] feather, stork.

H2625.definition:
from H2628 (חָסַל);
the ravager, i.e. a locust
KJV: caterpillar.

H2626.definition:
from H2630 (חָסַן);
properly, firm, i.e. (by implication) mighty
KJV: strong.

H2627.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2637 (חָסֵר);
deficient
KJV: wanting.

H2628.definition:
a primitive root;
to eat off
KJV: consume.

H2629.definition:
a primitive root;
to muzzle; by analogy, to stop the nose
KJV: muzzle, stop.

H2630.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to (be) compact; by implication, to hoard
KJV: lay up.

H2631.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2630 (חָסַן);
to hold in occupancy
KJV: possess.

H2633.definition:
from H2630 (חָסַן);
wealth
KJV: riches, strength, treasure.

H2635.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to that of H2636 (חַסְפַּס);
a clod
KJV: clay.

H2636.definition:
reduplicated from an unused root meaning apparently to peel;
a shred or scale
KJV: round thing.

H2637.definition:
a primitive root;
to lack; by implication, to fail, want, lessen
KJV: be abated, bereave, decrease, (cause to) fail, (have) lack, make lower, want.

H2638.definition:
from H2637 (חָסֵר);
lacking; hence, without
KJV: destitute, fail, lack, have need, void, want.

H2639.definition:
from H2637 (חָסֵר);
lack; hence, destitution
KJV: poverty, want.

H2640.definition:
from H2637 (חָסֵר);
poverty
KJV: in want of.

H2643.definition:
from H2653 (חׇפַף) (in the moral sense of covered from soil);
pure
KJV: innocent.

H2644.definition:
an orthographical variation of H2645 (חָפָה);
properly, to cover, i.e. (in a sinister sense) to act covertly
KJV: do secretly.

H2645.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2644 (חָפָא), H2653 (חׇפַף));
to cover; by implication, to veil, to encase, protect
KJV: ceil, cover, overlay.

H2646.definition:
from H2645 (חָפָה);
a canopy
KJV: chamber, closet, defence.

H2647.definition:
the same as H2646 (חֻפָּה);
Chuppah, an Israelite
KJV: Huppah.

H2648.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to start up suddenly, i.e. (by implication) to hasten away, to fear
KJV: (make) haste (away), tremble.

H2649.definition:
from H2468 (חֻלְדָּה);
hasty flight
KJV: haste.

H2650.definition:
plural of H2646 (חֻפָּה) (compare H2349 (חוּפָם));
Chuppim, an Israelite
KJV: Huppim.

H2651.definition:
from an unused root of uncertain signification;
a fist (only in the dual)
KJV: fists, (both) hands, hand(-ful).

H2652.definition:
from H2651 (חֹפֶן); perhaps pugilist;
Chophni, an Israelite
KJV: Hophni.

H2653.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2645 (חָפָה), H3182 (יָחֵף));
to cover (in protection)
KJV: cover.

H2654.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to incline to; by implication (literally but rarely) to bend; figuratively, to be pleased with, desire
KJV: [idiom] any at all, (have, take) delight, desire, favour, like, move, be (well) pleased, have pleasure, will, would.

H2655.definition:
from H2654 (חָפֵץ);
pleased with
KJV: delight in, desire, favour, please, have pleasure, whosoever would, willing, wish.

H2656.definition:
from H2654 (חָפֵץ);
pleasure; hence (abstractly) desire; concretely, a valuable thing; hence (by extension) a matter (as something in mind)
KJV: acceptable, delight(-some), desire, things desired, matter, pleasant(-ure), purpose, willingly.

H2657.definition:
from H2656 (חֵפֶץ) with suffixes; my delight (is) in her;
Cheptsi-bah, a fanciful name for Palestine
KJV: Hephzi-bah.

H2658.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to pry into; by implication, to delve, to explore
KJV: dig, paw, search out, seek.

H2659.definition:
a primitive root (perhaps rather the same as H2658 (חָפַר) through the idea of detection);
to blush; figuratively, to be ashamed, disappointed; causatively, to shame, reproach
KJV: be ashamed, be confounded, be brought to confusion (unto shame), come (be put to) shame, bring reproach.

H2660.definition:
from H2658 (חָפַר) or H2659 (חָפֵר); a pit of shame;
Chepher, a place in Palestine; also the name of three Israelites
KJV: Hepher.

H2661.definition:
from H2658 (חָפַר); a hole; only in connection with H6512 (פֵּרָה), which ought rather to be joined as one word, thus חַפַרְפֵּרָה; by reduplication from H2658 (חָפַר);
a burrower, i.e. probably a rat
KJV: [phrase] mole.

H2662.definition:
patronymically from H2660 (חֵפֶר);
a Chephrite (collectively) or descendants of Chepher
KJV: Hepherites.

H2663.definition:
dual of H2660 (חֵפֶר); double pit;
Chapharajim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Haphraim.

H2664.definition:
a primitive root;
to seek; causatively, to conceal oneself (i.e. let be sought), or mask
KJV: change, (make) diligent (search), disquise self, hide, search (for, out).

H2665.definition:
from H2664 (חָפַשׂ);
something covert, i.e. a trick
KJV: search.

H2666.definition:
a primitive root;
to spread loose; figuratively, to manumit
KJV: be free.

H2667.definition:
from H2666 (חָפַשׁ);
something spread loosely, i.e. a carpet
KJV: precious.

H2668.definition:
from H2666 (חָפַשׁ);
liberty (from slavery)
KJV: freedom.

H2670.definition:
from H2666 (חָפַשׁ);
exempt (from bondage, tax or care)
KJV: free, liberty.

H2671.definition:
from H2686 (חָצַץ); also by interchange for H6086 (עֵץ)
properly, a piercer, i.e. an arrow; by implication, a wound; figuratively, (of God) thunderbolt; the shaft of aspear
KJV: [phrase] archer, arrow, dart, shaft, staff, wound.

H2672.definition:
or חָצֵב; a primitive root;
to cut or carve (wood, stone or other material); by implication, to hew, split, square, quarry, engrave
KJV: cut, dig, divide, grave, hew (out, -er), made, mason.

H2673.definition:
a primitive root (compare H2086 (זֵד)));
to cut or split in two; to halve
KJV: divide, [idiom] live out half, reach to the midst, participle

H2674.definition:
a collective form of H2691 (חָצֵר); village;
Chatsor, the name (thus simply) of two places in Palestine and of one in Arabia
KJV: Hazor.

H2675.definition:
from H2674 (חָצוֹר) and a Aramaizing form of the feminine of H2319 (חָדָשׁ) (compare H2323 (חֲדָת));
new Chatsor, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hazor, Hadattah (as if two places).

H2676.definition:
from H2673 (חָצָה)lemma חָעָה ayin, corrected to חָצָה;
the middle (of the night)
KJV: mid(-night).

H2677.definition:
from H2673 (חָצָה)lemma חָעָה ayin, corrected to חָצָה;
the half or middle
KJV: half, middle, mid(-night), midst, part, two parts.

H2678.definition:
or חֵצִי; prolongation from H2671 (חֵץ);
an arrow
KJV: arrow.

H2679.definition:
from H2677 (חֵצִי) and the plural of H4496 (מְנוּחָה), with the article interposed; midst of the resting-places;
Chatsi-ham-Menuchoth, an Israelite
KJV: half of the Manahethites.

H2680.definition:
patronymically from H2679 (חֲצִי הַמְּנֻחוֹת);
a Chatsi-ham-Menachtite or descendant of Chatsi-ham-Menuchoth
KJV: half of the Manahethites.

H2681.definition:
a collateral form of H2691 (חָצֵר);
a court or abode
KJV: court.

H2682.definition:
perhaps originally the same as H2681 (חָצִיר), from the greenness of a courtyard;
grass; also a leek (collectively)
KJV: grass, hay, herb, leek.

H2683.definition:
from an unused root meaning to hold firmly;
the bosom (as comprised between the arms)
KJV: bosom.

H2684.definition:
a collateral form of H2683 (חֵצֶן), and meaning the same
{the bosom (as comprised between the arms)}
KJV: arm, lap.

H2685.definition:
(Aramaic) a primitive root;
properly, to shear or cut close; figuratively, to be severe
KJV: hasty, be urgent.

H2687.definition:
from H2687 (חָצָץ);  also like H2671 (חֵץ)
properly, something cutting; hence, gravel (as grit); an arrow
KJV: arrow, gravel (stone).

H2688.definition:
or חַצֲצֹן תָּמָר; from H2686 (חָצַץ) and H8558 (תָּמָר); division (i.e. perhaps row) of (the) palm-tree;
Chatsetson-tamar, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hazezon-tamar.

H2689.definition:
by reduplication from H2690 (חָצַר);
a trumpet (from its sundered or quavering note)
KJV: trumpet(-er).

H2690.definition:
a primitive root; properly, to surround with a stockade, and thus separate from the open country; but used only in the reduplicated form חֲצֹצֵר; or (2 Chronicles 5:12) חֲצֹרֵר; as dem. from H2689 (חֲצֹצְרָה);
to trumpet, i.e. blow on that instrument
KJV: blow, sound, trumpeter.

H2691.definition:
(masculine and feminine); from H2690 (חָצַר) in its original sense;
a yard (as inclosed by a fence); also a hamlet (as similarly surrounded with walls)
KJV: court, tower, village.

H2692.definition:
from H2691 (חָצֵר) and H146 (אַדָּר); (the) village of Addar;
Chatsar-Addar, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hazar-addar.

H2693.definition:
from H2691 (חָצֵר) and a feminine of H1408 (גַּד); (the) village of (female) Fortune;
Chatsar-Gaddah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hazar-gaddah.

H2694.definition:
from H2691 (חָצֵר) and H8484 (תִּיכוֹן) with the article interposed; village of the middle;
Chatsar-hat-Tikon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hazar-hatticon.

H2695.definition:
by an orthographical variation for H2696 (חֶצְרוֹן); enclosure;
Chetsro, an Israelite
KJV: Hezro, Hezrai.

H2696.definition:
from H2691 (חָצֵר); court-yard;
Chetsron, the name of a place in Palestine; also of two Israelites
KJV: Hezron.

H2697.definition:
patronymically from H2696 (חֶצְרוֹן);
a Chetsronite or (collectively) descendants of Chetsron
KJV: Hezronites.

H2698.definition:
feminine plural of H2691 (חָצֵר); yards;
Chatseroth, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hazeroth.

H2699.definition:
plural masculine of H2691 (חָצֵר); yards;
Chatserim, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hazerim.
